    <h2>How to AAnalyze a Residential Rental Property Deal</h2>
    <p>Successful real estate investing requires separating emotional appeal from cold financial fundamentals. Professional real estate investors rely on five core metrics to evaluate prospective income properties: <strong>Gross Yield</strong>, <strong>Net Operating Income (NOI)</strong>, <strong>Cap Rate</strong>, <strong>Monthly Net Cash Flow</strong>, and <strong>Cash-on-Cash Return</strong>.</p>

    <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:1.25rem 0;font-size:.9rem;">
      <thead>
        <tr style="background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e;">
          <th style="padding:10px 12px;border:1px solid #fde68a;text-align:left;">Investment Rule / Metric</th>
          <th style="padding:10px 12px;border:1px solid #fde68a;text-align:left;">Formula / Definition</th>
