    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <p>A thorough rental property analysis checks five numbers: <strong>gross yield</strong> (screens the market), <strong>cap rate</strong> (compares properties), <strong>NOI</strong> (lender and valuation metric), <strong>cash flow</strong> (monthly profitability), and <strong>cash-on-cash return</strong> (return on your specific investment).</p>
    <p>At 2026 rates (~7%), most properties need a gross yield above 9–10% to produce positive monthly cash flow with conventional financing. Focus on markets where rent-to-price ratios are strong: Cleveland OH, Memphis TN, Cincinnati OH, Indianapolis IN, and Birmingham AL.</p>
